#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063947 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064360 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68cd4840-bb77-5065-884a-ce1c8c309cd0" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Fraction of Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "78675372-1e29-5088-8907-52d9e54124e1" :question/math-academy-id "e-13083" :question/problem "What is $\\dfrac {\\left(\\dfrac 1 4\\right)} {\\left(-\\dfrac 3 7\\right)}$ expressed as a single fraction?" :question/worked-solution "First, remember that a fraction represents a division. So, a fraction of fractions is a division of two fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n((\\frac{1}{4}))/((-\\frac{3}{7})) &= \\frac{1}{4} \\div (-\\frac{3}{7})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that dividing by\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{3}{7}\n$$\n\nis the same as multiplying by its reciprocal\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{7}{3}\n$$\n\nWe can use this fact to simplify the fraction above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{4} \\div (-\\frac{3}{7}) &=  \\\\\n\\frac{1}{4} \\cdot (-\\frac{7}{3}) &=  \\\\\n- \\frac{1 \\cdot 7}{4 \\cdot 3} &=  \\\\\n&= - \\frac{7}{12}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n((\\frac{1}{4}))/((-\\frac{3}{7})) &= -\\frac{7}{12}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we used the fact that a positive number times a negative number gives a negative number."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063948 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064361 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ca49b4e-a4fa-5a67-9334-12e8656b5d1a" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Counting Number by a Fraction"}] :question/id #uuid "3bad12f4-14b2-5ab6-a1db-9d460b9a26ca" :question/math-academy-id "e-13084" :question/problem "Simplify $\\dfrac{\\left(-3\\right)} {\\left(-\\dfrac 3 5\\right)}$." :question/worked-solution "First, remember that a fraction represents a division:\n\n$$\n((-3))/((-\\frac{3}{5})) =-3 \\div (-\\frac{3}{5})\n$$\n\nNow, recall that\n\n$$\n-3 =-\\dfrac{3}{1}\n$$\n\nand dividing by\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nis the same as multiplying by its reciprocal\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{5}{3}\n$$\n\nWe can use these facts to simplify the fraction above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(-3) \\div (-\\frac{3}{5}) &=  \\\\\n(-\\frac{3}{1}) \\div (-\\frac{3}{5}) &=  \\\\\n(-\\frac{3}{1}) \\cdot (-\\frac{5}{3}) &=  \\\\\n\\frac{3 \\cdot 5}{1 \\cdot 3} &=  \\\\\n\\frac{15}{3} &=  \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\left(-3\\right)} {\\left(-\\dfrac 3 5\\right)} = 5\n$$\n\nNotice that we used the fact that a negative number times a negative number gives a positive number."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063949 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064362 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56936b9b-2b52-58a7-ae3f-7d51492b8247" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Fraction by a Counting Number"}] :question/id #uuid "87974d27-c494-5b1a-84e9-03e39f3e0b1c" :question/math-academy-id "e-13086" :question/problem "Calculate $\\dfrac{\\left(-\\dfrac 3 2\\right)}{6}$." :question/worked-solution "We can use either of the following two methods.\n\n**Method 1 - The Long Way**\n\nFirst, remember that a fraction represents a division:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\left(-\\dfrac 3 2\\right)}{6} = \\left(-\\dfrac 3 2\\right) \\div 6\n$$\n\nNow, recall that dividing by $6$ is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nWe can use this fact to simplify the fraction above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(-\\frac{3}{2}) \\div 6 &=  \\\\\n(-\\frac{3}{2}) \\cdot (\\frac{1}{6}) &=  \\\\\n- \\frac{3 \\cdot 1}{2 \\cdot 6} &=  \\\\\n&= - \\frac{3}{12}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{3}{12} =-\\dfrac{3 \\div 3}{12 \\div 3} = -\\dfrac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\left(-\\dfrac 3 2\\right)}{6}= -\\dfrac14\n$$\n\n**Method 2 - The Quick Way**\n\nThe result will have the same numerator as the top fraction, and the denominator is just the product of the two denominators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n((-\\frac{3}{2}))/(6) &=  \\\\\n\\frac{-3}{2 \\cdot 6} &=  \\\\\n- \\frac{3}{12} &=  \\\\\n- \\frac{3 \\div 3}{12 \\div 3} &=  \\\\\n&= - \\frac{1}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064776 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064361 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ca49b4e-a4fa-5a67-9334-12e8656b5d1a" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Counting Number by a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf05019e-0fbb-5909-bdc7-441afa5579c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062714} {:answer/id #uuid "d4630dd5-db80-5a2c-8abb-69a118e71dfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062715} {:answer/id #uuid "e391f5b4-0444-5612-9d5d-cfb8b9723815" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062716} {:answer/id #uuid "556d0f48-496d-5b83-a01c-ed647970c8c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062717} {:answer/id #uuid "644225ae-897f-5530-9615-d488c54d900a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062718}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c0296223-0afa-55c4-985e-ee00bd370614" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062713}] :question/id #uuid "6c3cdbb7-2f20-5471-9a71-577081e6a156" :question/math-academy-id "q-43479" :question/problem "What is $(3)/((\\frac{7}{3}))$?"}]}
